course: dictionary
lesson: 3019
title: Dynamic: a word with many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word dynamic changes its meaning depending on where you meet it. The words around it are its context, and they tell you which meaning fits. «Dynamic pricing» means raising prices when demand is high, that is, when lots of people want to buy. The clue is high demand: the price goes up as more people want something.
explain: As an adjective, dynamic means full of energy, ideas and enthusiasm, or always changing, moving or growing. A dynamic leader is lively and gets things done. Ask yourself: what word would fit here? If you can swap in lively or always changing and the sentence still makes sense, you have found the meaning.
explain: Dynamic also has special meanings in other subjects. In music, dynamics are how loud or soft the music is played. In science, dynamics is the part of physics about forces and how they make things move. When you see dynamic in a science or music lesson, look at the subject around it to choose the right meaning.
fact: Dynamic (adjective) means full of energy, ideas and enthusiasm, or always changing, moving or growing.
fact: «Dynamic pricing» means raising prices when demand is high, when lots of people want to buy.
fact: In music, dynamics are how loud or soft the music is played, such as piano (soft) and forte (loud).
fact: In science, dynamics is the part of physics about forces and how they make things move.
fact: A dynamic can also be the way people or things act on each other in a group, as in «group dynamics» or «team dynamic».
exercise: «The new coach is a dynamic leader who never stops.» What does dynamic mean here? | Very old and slow | Hidden under the water | Quiet and still | *Full of energy and ideas
exercise: In music class, the teacher talks about the dynamics of the piece. What are dynamics in music? | Lists of the instruments in the band | *How loud or soft the music is played | The name of the person who wrote the music
exercise: «Dynamic pricing» means raising prices when demand is high. When do the prices go up? | When the shop is closed | At midnight every day | *When lots of people want to buy | When nobody wants to buy
test:
Leo says dynamic in science means lively and full of energy. What does dynamics mean in science? | A type of music played very loudly | *The part of physics about forces and how things move | The way a group of people get along with each other | A kind of shop that changes its prices
test:
«The team's dynamic changed after the new player joined.» What does dynamic mean as a noun here? | *The way people act on each other in a group | The loud sound of a drum | A list of the team's scores | A very old map of the playing field
exam: «The dynamic teacher kept the class moving with new games,» and in a music lesson the piano teacher asks, «Play the dynamics of this piece.» Which meaning of dynamic fits each use? | Hidden, then a type of rhythm | Quiet, then the name of a song | Very old, then a list of notes | *Full of energy and ideas, then how loud or soft the music is played
